 it to the limits of what's usable as a  phone but it's nice because it's a  relatively thin bezel and you'll see  that it's thinner than the bezel of some  other phones like the galaxy s3 so it  doesn't really push the physical size of  the phone too big here it is in my hand  i'm about six foot two and i've shown  this before you guys have seen it i can  use the note 2 as a one-handed device  although it is quite difficult to sneak  a text maybe during class when your  phone's display is so big  but i've been told that i have really  large hands and i know that's true so  here it is in my mom's hand she's about  five foot five and was quoted saying  that this is simply too big to be a  phone so for her if you have small hands  you might want to make this a two-handed  device and consider that it's probably  always going to be a two-handed device  for you but if you have larger hands or  maybe just kind of semi-large hands if  you're anywhere over 510 this is  probably going to be okay as a  one-handed regular phone use which is  pretty neat so here it is next to some  other phones including the samsung  galaxy s3 which you've probably seen in  person at some point  and here it is next to the nexus 7 and  yes it is definitely still smaller than  a small tablet it also fits in the  pocket just fine i can vouch for  anything that's not skinny jeans and  also here's how it looks next to my head  while taking a phone call i actually  don't think it looks all that insane  some people thought it would but  especially from a normal distance away  you probably couldn't tell the  difference between that and a galaxy s3  another super common question i get is  about the display is it good enough i  mean it's big but is it good the droid  dna just became the first somewhat  popular phone with a 1080p display i can  almost guarantee that the galaxy note 3  in the second half of this year will  have a 1080p hd samsung display but i  honestly really like the note 2's  display it's not the brightest in the  world and the viewing angles are pretty  good they're not bad they're ammo led  displays but the point is it's big it's  a big clear beautiful display that  really makes this device people also  want to know about the stylus and to be  honest i just now use it occasionally  one for guester typing on the android  jelly bean keyboard that's been my  biggest use of the stylus super super  fast and very accurate and i also  started using s note just a little bit  but not for anything too intensive i  found it handy just to take random notes  during a phone call people also want to  know how is touchwiz holding up are you  gonna root it well i said before and  i'll say it again when given the choice  i prefer stock android no skin but if i  have to choose a skin i'll use touchwiz  pretty much every time it's still  running on top of android 4.1 jelly bean  here it's buttery smooth it takes  advantage of the screen size and the  stylus as well so yeah it's nice i'm  okay with it but when the black one  comes out i absolutely will root and put  cyanogenmod 10.1 on it and run a super  nexus with android 4.2 but this is the  titanium one so not yet also the little  things yes the camera is still very  high-end it takes great photos i share  them all the time on twitter and still  take some of the best 1080p videos of  any smartphone out there so it's  definitely worth it if you're in it for  the camera and yes the speaker is still  very loud and yes i did put a sticker  over the ugly verizon home button  branding i had to do that and yes the  battery life still lasts hours beyond my  expectations all the time it is still a  beast of a phone so in the end it's not  your average popular smartphone it's  popular for more reasons than just the  specs and what's on the inside the form  factor offers an experience that no  other smartphone out there currently  does and i can still recommend it for  that reason so in conclusion i don't  always get asked